{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fppf}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80bfcee3d0a45bc668196cd3cd8784636ed6a86ae9611778202133774690d0ff", "source_text": "Fppf topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:822d703eea8d72526476864762fd0b6fb7e3cb1479ca0c8dafa4c152f684901e", "unit_id": "tag:03Y7:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-fppf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:38b0af62c513ff47232ea1932815db3f296f7dadc8e174bc9f6db1cc1b7853f9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss the notion of an fppf covering of algebraic spaces,\nand we define the big fppf site of an algebraic space. Please compare with\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7e684145b8c156124a33cfde8f9466cc7218e05037b2ebb66569de198e500b93", "unit_id": "tag:03Y7:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n|X| = \\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I} |f_i|(|X_i|),\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-fppf-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e76fae56c3226e3151fabee0092a70b466b5acf08f6f31c1ff32db92d85286f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10ed9c8f80f72af444fad4d1b9732926ab2526fd7a219e96564c6b221f7e5f9c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nAn <TEXTITOPEN_0001>fppf covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is flat and locally of finite presentation\nand such that\n<MATH_0008>\ni.e., the morphisms are jointly surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3321a9b84e4477889b4432ecd84b791501815f0c7f51e67a535b1f5dd6120aea", "unit_id": "tag:03Y8:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-fppf-covering}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:471134057d0984d44af5a155ac2d0e8da290e691491a26f5be3167e4b5c64d48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4f9323433fa0bd277481c9abb8084a068651437aaa83b71f4e408bfa0ab9bbaf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is exactly the same as\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0001> and all the <MATH_0002> are schemes, then we recover the usual\nnotion of an fppf covering of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:02596899b3a5375fdab9d9cbb86a2048d92dfcaf6c852c7d794d4ba91e7d67c0", "unit_id": "tag:03Y7:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ada2fe451f30c8cef738a1ef34dfff3d68bb13c00e849c40eabcd059b0f53bbe", "source_text": "Any syntomic covering is an fppf covering, and a fortiori,\nany smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale, or Zariski covering is an fppf covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e54a07aa3f14b9b56c948804c03ea2ce48effbeac31a35a8a6732606055a838b", "unit_id": "tag:0DFC:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-syntomic-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-syntomic-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c8ce6955ef01b4a63cc25041324de5828bbf15be9bcee4d2568080016d2704d", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions, the fact that a syntomic morphism\nis flat and locally of finite presentation\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>) and\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b3cb473af92f0270ff59435fef3146e3b89ab5ccd2e5daf1237ee7618fe7bddd", "unit_id": "tag:0DFC:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X' \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{X' \\times_X X_i \\to X'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e3d9a30bc295880eafea81ddede5c59549b2394c91422582e284bba1fee4680", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82683483d40bfc6f5469f590fc896b58029f6fef7d76590a25fcd5a6d0b7a63f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0005>\nis an fppf covering of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is an fppf covering and for each\n<MATH_0008> we have an fppf covering <MATH_0009>, then\n<MATH_0010> is an fppf covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is an fppf covering\nand <MATH_0012> is a morphism of algebraic spaces then\n<MATH_0013> is an fppf covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9918605b0fcf04babdf974632818d034c645479b20cd22300e221d109c0ffb61", "unit_id": "tag:03Y9:statement"}
